<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1949</h1><p class="ref-lede">1949 in world history: 48 events, 18 births, 21 deaths, 7 works, 9 states founded and 14 that came to an end. 445 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1945">1945</a><a href="/years/1946">1946</a><a href="/years/1947">1947</a><a href="/years/1948">1948</a><a href="/years/1949" aria-current="page">1949</a><a href="/years/1950">1950</a><a href="/years/1951">1951</a><a href="/years/1952">1952</a><a href="/years/1953">1953</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-30">30 March</a> · Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan-day">Rajasthan Day</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Rajasthan Day is a public holiday in the Indian state of Rajasthan, celebrated on 30 March.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-4">4 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Twelve nations sign the North Atlantic Treaty</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Foreign ministers meeting in Washington signed the treaty that created <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a>, committing members to treat an attack on one as an attack on all. The alliance anchored Western defence through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-12">12 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Soviet Union lifts the Berlin Blockade</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">After almost eleven months, Soviet authorities reopened road and rail routes into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-berlin">West Berlin</a>. The Allied airlift that had supplied the city became a defining episode of the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-8">8 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Orwell's Nineteen Eighty-Four is published</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Secker and Warburg published <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-orwell">George Orwell</a>'s novel of a totalitarian surveillance state. Terms such as 'Big Brother' and 'doublethink' passed into everyday language.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-29">29 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Soviet Union tests its first atomic bomb</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The USSR exploded its first atomic bomb at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/semey">Semipalatinsk</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazakhstan">Kazakhstan</a>, years earlier than the West expected. The American nuclear monopoly was over and the arms race had begun.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/beijing" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/beijing.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-1">1 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Mao Zedong proclaims the People's Republic of China</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">From the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiananmen">Gate of Heavenly Peace</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mao-zedong">Mao Zedong</a> proclaimed the founding of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a>. Communist victory in the civil war placed the world's most populous country under a new regime.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/indonesian-independence" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/indonesian-independence.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/indonesian-independence">Indonesian independence</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Indonesian independence was proclaimed in 1945 and recognised by the Netherlands in 1949 after a period of armed conflict and negotiation.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-indonesian-round-table-conference" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dutch-indonesian-round-table-conference.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/dutch-indonesian-round-table-conference">Dutch–Indonesian Round Table Conference</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Dutch–Indonesian Round Table Conference met in The Hague from August to November 1949, bringing together the Netherlands, the Republic of Indonesia and the federal states created by the Dutch.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-guningtou">Battle of Guningtou</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Guningtou was fought on Kinmen island, off the Fujian coast, from 25 to 27 October 1949.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/proclamation-of-the-peoples-republic-of-china" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/proclamation-of-the-peoples-republic-of-china.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/proclamation-of-the-peoples-republic-of-china">Proclamation of the People's Republic of China</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The People's Republic of China was proclaimed by Mao Zedong, chairman of the Chinese Communist Party, on 1 October 1949 in Tiananmen Square in Beijing, a ceremony that also proclaimed the Central People's Government and marked the foundation of contemporary…</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/elysee-accords">Élysée Accords</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Élysée Accords were agreements signed on 8 March 1949 by the French President Vincent Auriol and the former emperor Bảo Đại.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/bevin-sforza-plan">Bevin–Sforza plan</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Bevin–Sforza plan was a proposal agreed in May 1949 by the British foreign secretary Ernest Bevin and the Italian foreign minister Carlo Sforza for the future of Italy's former colony of Libya.</p></div></li></ol></section>
